
# <type>(<scope>): <imperative summary, at most 72 characters>
# A subject alone is enough for an obvious small change.
# Otherwise add a blank line and a short paragraph explaining what changed
# and why. Include approach, decisions, tests, or references only when useful.
# Why / How / Log / Test / Refs are considerations, not required headers.
# Omit filler, empty labels, thinking-method names, and routine placeholders.
# State material verification limits; never invent results.
# Optional work-item trailer: Refs: #123
# Avoid bare #123 lines; default Git comment cleanup removes them.
# Use resolution wording only when intended and the workflow is verified.
# These guidance comments are removed by default Git commit cleanup.
